{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgorKHNy4kCSXVe8yjKru","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've gone through all ten screenshots. Here's my answer and the report.\n\n**What I'd tell a colleague:** It's actually upfront about this, which I didn't expect. There's a whole page for it (\"מה האתר עוד לא מכסה\"). By its own red banner, nothing on that list is calculated yet: \"עד שייסגרו, האתר לא מחשב אותם\". That covers gold (ETC, LBMA, gold ETFs), corporate and Bonds-Israel bonds, debt restructurings, structured products and deposits, foreign-currency deposits and accounts, the FX fee (עמלת חליפין), currency-hedged funds, digital money-market wallets, investment-linked life insurance, managers' insurance, insurance funds and קרן י', annuity commutation and the 190 track, REITs, robo-advisors, and a few more. Then there's a second list of things it won't ever do: stock picking, trading and derivatives, loans, physical real estate, ranking by past returns, and executing anything. So my single tech stocks are out for good. The FX rate I pay my broker is on the \"not calculated yet\" list. Plain index ETFs aren't on either list, so I assume those are covered, but this page doesn't say so outright. I'm fairly sure of all this. What decided it was the banner plus the red \"לא מחושב\" tag on every card. Bottom line: for my US ETFs it might be useful. For FX costs or anything with a policy wrapper, not yet.\n\n**What I looked at, in order:**\n1. The header, subtitle and red banner.\n2. The card titles and the red tags, as I scrolled.\n3. The \"מצב הכיסוי\" folds, because they're about method. Each one shows what's blocking (an open question like how gold ETFs or foreign-currency deposit interest are taxed), what's been resolved, and a line saying the item will appear in the guide and comparison pages once it's closed.\n4. The \"won't compare and won't do\" list at the bottom.\n5. The footer: \"אישי, לא מסחרי, בלי קישורי שיווק\". No broker name anywhere, which is good.\n\n**What I skimmed or skipped:** I skimmed the definitions (\"מה ידוע\") and skipped all the law and regulation citations (חוק ניירות ערך and the rest) and the source dates.\n\n**Where I hesitated or wasn't sure:**\n- The struck-out \"נסגר ב־24.10.2026\" lines: I read them as questions already resolved, but crossing them out looks like they were cancelled.\n- The codes MF-28, TX2-01 and TXA-28 aren't explained.\n- The orange \"לפי החברה\" tag: does it mean the data is self-reported by the company?\n- Nothing on this page states which products *are* covered, so I'm inferring that from what's missing.\n\n**What bothered me:**\n- It's a wall of cards with no table and no filter. There's no single view of \"covered / partly covered / not covered\".\n- Every card says \"לא מחושב\", so nothing distinguishes an item that's one question away from done from one that's barely started.\n- Nothing about the monthly account fee or broker FX spreads beyond a one-line definition. That's exactly the money I'm probably leaving on the table.\n\n**Would I have closed the tab?** Not on this page; it answers the question. But it gave me nothing to compare with what I pay today, so I'd go to \"השקעה במדד\" next and close it there if no fee numbers show up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3682,"cache_read_input_tokens":18768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3682},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"029ed6d3-a852-4155-b3e0-fe576b91f9c3","uuid":"d3870986-8185-4077-be0a-f4c3c8c23728","timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:04:12.037Z","request_id":"req_011CgorKH7qymuNUQqssopwB"}
